  "prefactor_note": "Fixed-rate deflation ln eps + (4*pi/q)*mu = A + B*ln(mu): chi3 gives A=5.63, B=2.09 (rms 0.117). The ln-mu exponent B sits squarely in the band of the other four systems (chi4 2.07, dh 1.99, chi5 1.03, zeta 5.53), i.e. the chi3 prefactor is a slowly growing polynomial of the same prolate/Fuchs shape as the RH-true controls; zeta remains the sole outlier in B, attributable to its q=1 endpoint status and the W02 pole term, not to chi3-visible arithmetic. No arithmetically meaningful deviation: the five B values show no pattern correlated with Euler-product integrity or RH status (RH-false DH sits BETWEEN the RH-true chi4 and chi5), so at this resolution the arithmetic-hides-in-prefactors loophole gains no support from the fifth point -- though fully closing it still needs the dedicated higher-resolution prefactor study flagged in ccm-dh-filter.json (more lambda points, fixed N/dps schedule)."
 },
